This fix is Alloy 6 compliant because it removes the syntactically invalid function declarations and leverages Alloy's built-in total ordering utilities for Time, as the user specified.

[LESSON]:
When defining orderings in Alloy, prefer util/ordering for total order relations instead of custom functions, and always specify function return types and bodies correctly per Alloy 6 syntax.
