3. Can't use "if-then-else" directly in Alloy 6 facts or predicates → Must use implication (=>) or conditional expressions in let bindings.
4. Can't use 'if ... then ... else ...' expressions in Alloy 6 → Must use 'condition => expr1 else expr2' conditional operator instead.
5. Alloy syntax requires global relations to be declared within signatures; attempting to declare global mutable relations with `var` outside signatures causes syntax errors blocking all verification.

