The syntax error occurs at line 168 in the pred R1R2 block, specifically at the let binding: let sEnd := {s: State | ...} |. Alloy 6 does not allow a let binding to be followed immediately by a vertical bar (|), as this is valid only in quantifiers (all, some, etc.), not in let expressions. The intent seems to be to introduce a local variable sEnd (a set of State), then use it in the subsequent Boolean formula. Previous failed fixes focused on changing := versus =, or on bracketing, but none addressed that Alloy 6 requires let ... = ... { ... } (curly braces) to delimit the let-bound scope for multi-line or compound expressions.

[FIX INTENT]:
Encapsulate the let binding and its dependent expressions within curly braces to create a valid Alloy 6 let-block.

[REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS]:
