### RELEVANT LESSONS LEARNED:

Previous Lessons:
1. Alloy syntax requires global relations to be declared within signatures; attempting to declare global mutable relations with `var` outside signatures causes syntax errors blocking all verification.
2. - Syntax errors in relational navigation using incorrect set comprehension block all verification; relational dot notation is the Alloy standard and critical for progress.
3. Alloy requires careful bracketing for multiline conditional expressions; failure to enclose such expressions causes syntax errors blocking verification.
4. - Alloy 6 requires `open` statements to be at the very beginning of the model, before any comments or code lines. Preceding comments can cause syntax errors.
5. - Alloy 6 requires `open` statements with parameters to use square brackets and be separated from the module name by a space.

