- Step 3: Remove the invalid "=> ... else ..." syntax entirely; do not attempt to use Alloy's "if ... then ... else ..." unless you use the correct ternary syntax (which would also be valid as an alternative, but the above is the simplest set comprehension).

[RATIONALE]:
This approach eliminates the misused implication/else construct and instead uses a set comprehension to define s.emergencyAdmins, which is valid Alloy 6 syntax and avoids the previously failed attempts at patching with parentheses, let, or implication constructs.

[LESSON]:
When needing to assign a set conditionally based on the existence of certain objects, use set comprehensions in Alloy; do not attempt to use "=> ... else ..." for value assignment—Alloy does not support that syntax.

